{"duration_api_ms":5501,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"941e1ed0-6a38-4e9b-97b4-d89ee2e961ce","total_cost_usd":0.0007466,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":345},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1249,"outputTokens":961,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":706,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0007466,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":531,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":706,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"No. Historical exchange volume shows only the secondary-market trading that has already occurred, and it can understate liquidity. Much of an ETF's tradable capacity sits in the creation/redemption process. Authorized participants (APs) can create or redeem shares in large blocks, typically 25,000 to 100,000 shares, by delivering or receiving the underlying basket or cash. This arbitrage tends to keep the price close to NAV, but only when the underlying securities are liquid enough for APs to trade them efficiently.\n\nAdditional indicators to examine:\n\n- **Quoted and effective spreads**, and how they vary through the day\n- **Displayed depth** at the NBBO and across price levels\n- **Premium or discount** to intraday indicative NAV (iNAV) and to end-of-day NAV\n- **Underlying basket liquidity**: constituent spreads, daily volume, and market depth\n- **Creation/redemption activity** and shares outstanding changes\n- **Number and quality of market makers and APs**\n- **Auction and closing volume**, which often dominate for passive flows\n- **Behavior during past stress periods**, such as March 2020\n\nExecution outcomes for a specific order depend on current conditions and should be assessed with pre-trade analysis.","ttft_ms":2302,"type":"result","duration_ms":4358,"uuid":"b9be4f78-c9a8-4032-b612-b1192f1babfa","ttft_stream_ms":440,"time_to_request_ms":81,"first_content_frame_ms":440,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
